{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy","id":576222,"title":"Garou & Leech Kiss Ecstasy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-02T01:57:54-07:00","id":576222,"title":"Garou & Leech Kiss Ecstasy","content":"I ask this since I need it and I'm too lazy to remember where it is written!<br /> <br /> In the unfortunate and (maybe unlikely) situation of a Kindred biting a Garou...does the Garou suffer the the Kiss Ecstasy (and therefore stop fighting the Leech) or are the Garou immune to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T04:36:20-07:00","id":576270,"title":"","content":"Sadly, they are not immune, and will need to roll willpower (or spend willpower, i'm fuzzy on Vampire rules). However, the kiss is grounds for a frenzy roll for the Garou and that... will not end the Kiss on a good note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T08:30:31-07:00","id":576389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=576270#post576270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, they are not immune, and will need to roll willpower (or spend willpower, i'm fuzzy on Vampire rules). However, the kiss is grounds for a frenzy roll for the Garou and that... will not end the Kiss on a good note.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T09:46:31-07:00","id":576526,"title":"","content":"V20 rules say that strong-willed mortals (Willpower 9+) can try to resist and Kindred, regardless of Willpower, may make a Self Control/Instict roll (9).<br /> Given the above rules, it is clear that resisiting the ecstasy is incredibly difficult, even for Vampires.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Garou are not mentioned. They are not immortals ... but they are definitively not &quot;normal&quot; mortals!<br /> <br /> I'm tempted to allow Frenzy rolls, although this means making &quot;resisting ecstasy&quot; much easier for Garou than it is for Kindred, and we have no official info that this is true (am I wrong? please correct me!).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5960,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","user":"LucaCherstich","date":". 07-02-2015, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T12:14:04-07:00","id":576658,"title":"","content":"Frenzy is a quite regular reaction to intense emotional stimuli. And while it may be a &quot;defense&quot; it results in a murder spree... so it's not exactly without its flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T14:21:37-07:00","id":576774,"title":"","content":"Well, I guess that a Vampire who has fanged a Garou has already struggled a lot to do it (and not been dismembered) so a last minute Garou frenzy sounds like not a pleasant surprise for the undead....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T15:02:08-07:00","id":576800,"title":"","content":"I'm out on the road so I can't get the page numbers, but the story teller's guide to garou is very clear in that shifters do NOT count as mortals for any purpose in vampire powers/abilities. Treat as vampires with rage and will substituted for any virtues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 07-02-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T14:24:44-07:00","id":577785,"title":"","content":"Yeah -- pretty much what CeltSPZ says, with the caveat that they &quot;count as mortals&quot; for purposes of Dominate/Presence (they're affected by them, but may have Willpower/Gifts that allow for resistance or at least mitigation of &quot;x&quot; effects) and similarly applicable powers (except where noted). Basically, a werewolf is affected by The Kiss (and more-bemoan the poor garou who gets swarmed by several leeches and several of them &quot;get their bite on&quot;...), but they have a little extra &quot;oomph&quot; for working through it via Willpower and/or Rage/Frenzy, more so than most mortals (though *sooooo* many WW players forget that a garou can also fun &quot;Fox&quot; -- the equivalent of vampires' Rotschreck (sp) -- so a &quot;frenzy&quot; could well include the werewolf running with his tail between his legs... literally...; alternately, even if the Frenzy manifests as his turning into a killing machine, if the several bites example occur as above, he may well find himself in a situation similar to Akasha in the (horrible) movie version of &quot;Queen of the Damned&quot; -- the garou fights, but at the same time his energy is being drained, and possibly within just a round or two he finds himself completely drained or at least too diminished to fight -- enough aggro that even a death-rage roll can't overcome...).<br /> <br /> Important things to keep in mind....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":".  Spacing 07-03-2015, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T14:55:35-07:00","id":577799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucaCherstich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=576774#post576774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I guess that a Vampire who has fanged a Garou has already struggled a lot to do it (and not been dismembered) so a last minute Garou frenzy sounds like not a pleasant surprise for the undead....</div> </div> </div> </div>If you call wearing leather and black eyeliner &quot;struggled&quot;. Most Garou do not use Scent of the True Form or Sense Wyrm on every single person they meet in a nightclub.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T06:52:13-07:00","id":578685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=577799#post577799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you call wearing leather and black eyeliner &quot;struggled&quot;. Most Garou do not use Scent of the True Form or Sense Wyrm on every single person they meet in a nightclub.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they have incredible, non-human senses, so if that oddly cold and pale but fascinating and charming girl you have been flirting with in the nightclub start biting you while pretending to do something else .... if you are a Garou you should notice it &quot;a bit earlier&quot; than most normal mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5960,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","user":"LucaCherstich","date":". 07-04-2015, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:38:19-07:00","id":578871,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd be ok with a Primal urge roll to have the garou notice little warning signs like not blinking enough, cold skin, not sweating even though they're dancing a ton.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T18:10:47-07:00","id":579300,"title":"","content":"I would, for sure, but not if the vampire used Blush of Life. In this case she will do all of that, and it isn't uncommon, either, for vampires that hunt on nightclubs and such to do precisely that.<br /> <br /> A Rage roll would imply the werewolf reacts either with ecstasy or absolute revulsion. Not out of touch with the game, but maybe too much for some games or situations, so I don't know if I would use that. Maybe the ST should judge between Rage and Willpower based on circunstances?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T18:32:59-07:00","id":579309,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of a White Wolf novel where the protagonist was a Toreador living in Canada. He intimidated a human by just standing there in the winter, as the human noticed the steam coming from his breath and nothing coming from the vampire. Anywho....I think at the end of the day whatever is best for the game is best for the game. For me in my games it's 2 separate saves, a frenzy check followed by a will roll. Some may see that as much, but I'm running a werewolf game not a vampire one and my players have fun with it which is what really matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T21:46:20-07:00","id":579445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=579300#post579300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would, for sure, but not if the vampire used Blush of Life. In this case she will do all of that, and it isn't uncommon, either, for vampires that hunt on nightclubs and such to do precisely that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying this is canon, but it's something to think about<b></b>: even with Blush of Life, natural animals will tend to react negatively to vampires. So there is still the argument that a Primal Urge roll, to represent natural animal instincts would alert a Garou to something being wrong with the individual, even if they couldn't precisely decide why. and an sufficiently experienced Garou could almost certainly be able to pin down what those instincts mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T23:01:09-07:00","id":579493,"title":"","content":"In W20 primal urge got a huge beef up if you ask me...it's listed in the core on pg. 273-274 it feels like there are more things you can use that talent for such as detecting magically hidden objects/enemies. Its all about the animal in you noticing things humans have long since forgotten to notice. I play it up a lot in my game since W20. I'll admit before I was never quite sure how to use it (yet I always loaded my characters/npcs with it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T23:26:54-07:00","id":579501,"title":"","content":"Primal Urge as a hability in Apocalypse was a mistake, IMHO, but once it is there, I agree with the uses listed in W20.<br /> <br /> In this case, though, I don't use it for detecting vampires simple to keep things interesting. First because it doesn't sound right to me for a splat having the hability to know without effort about the presence of others. There are gifts to do that, if you want. Second it serves precisely to give more value to point-investment and action-investment on knowing things. Third giving this for free kills the mistery.<br /> <br /> Already played with a ST that used Primal Urge to give EVERYTHING to the werewolves. Theoreticaly it was a crossover game, but playing a vampire with this guy was almost a nightmare by itself.<br /> <br /> Either way, what best serves your game. But I would still keep it just to vamps using Obfuscate or Chimestry. Werewolfs AREN'T natural animals and having superb instincts isn't the same as being a natural animal. They're not more natural in this regard as a human being, and humans can't do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T13:45:17-07:00","id":580156,"title":"","content":"Using it to spot the lack of sweat, misting breath, lack of warmth in the flesh etc is legit because it's something that can be spotted and is probably something more likely to be registered by a Garou's Primal urge than just alertness (but can totally be spotted with alertness too, by anyone).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T15:38:38-07:00","id":580309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=580156#post580156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using it to spot the lack of sweat, misting breath, lack of warmth in the flesh etc is legit because it's something that can be spotted and is probably something more likely to be registered by a Garou's Primal urge than just alertness (but can totally be spotted with alertness too, by anyone).</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it doesn't outright say &quot;this is a vampire&quot;, on account of the existence of Risen and other walking corpses. It also won't answer the important question of &quot;what kind of vampire?&quot; that might crop up if using KotE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T23:32:01-07:00","id":580575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=579501#post579501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Already played with a ST that used Primal Urge to give EVERYTHING to the werewolves. Theoreticaly it was a crossover game, but playing a vampire with this guy was almost a nightmare by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Primal Urge can be used to detect things that are not right. But I would use a high difficulty number - 8 or 9 - to do so. And you would need to include a lot of other things such a roll would detect - that would not be correct in identifying actual monsters like vampires. A lupus might use a lower number to detect vampires, but it would work on the same things. There should be a LOT of &quot;false positives&quot; so that players can't rely on such abilities as fool proof.<br /> <br /> In other words, it could be a vampire. Or maybe someone with too much botox. Or with too much prozac. Or kept in doors in their corporate drone office job too long. Being a vampire should be way down on the list of the things that set off their Primal Urge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T23:42:56-07:00","id":580581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=580575#post580575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Primal Urge can be used to detect things that are not right. But I would use a high difficulty number - 8 or 9 - to do so. And you would need to include a lot of other things such a roll would detect - that would not be correct in identifying actual monsters like vampires. A lupus might use a lower number to detect vampires, but it would work on the same things. There should be a LOT of &quot;false positives&quot; so that players can't rely on such abilities as fool proof.<br /> <br /> In other words, it could be a vampire. Or maybe someone with too much botox. Or with too much prozac. Or kept in doors in their corporate drone office job too long. Being a vampire should be way down on the list of the things that set off their Primal Urge.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's looking dead from a double shift, and then there's completely lacking all signs of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T10:02:57-07:00","id":581121,"title":"","content":"Primal Urge should be natural instincts going wild saying something is wrong/off. It's how animals react to most vampires. Normal animals don't tend to have negative reactions to botox or prosac users.<br /> Generally, I would say any Garou with at least a Primal Urge of 2 or so should get a roll. And they most likely won't even know why they instinctively feel something is wrong with the person. I don't think Primal Urge should act like a vampire detector. I do think it should warrant having a similar reaction to a vampire that animals do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:45:27-07:00","id":581471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=581121#post581121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Primal Urge should act like a vampire detector. I do think it should warrant having a similar reaction to a vampire that animals do.</div> </div> </div> </div>How that aversion is displayed in game makes all the difference. Putting a little effort into it as a storyteller helps a lot.<br /> <br /> &quot;The gal at the end of the bar smells dead, probably a vampire,&quot; isn't how Primal Urge works, but more egregiously, it sucks as a way of conveying information. <br /> <br /> &quot;Clara's smile is radiant, and her laugh as easy as ever. She leans over to the bartender and orders a pair of whiskey shots as you return her glance and start toward her. Then you hesitate for a single unthinking heartbeat, your grin almost wilting into a snarl before you manage to crush the feeling and hunker down on a tired barstool. She shoves a brimming shot at you with a wink, and yet you don't reach for it, not right away. The whiskey is identical, the bar is just as you remember, and Clara- all but unchanged over the past five years. Something, <i>something</i> is off.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T19:30:13-07:00","id":581831,"title":"","content":"First, I would like to remember some people that we are talking about using Primal Urge to perceive vampires using the Brush of Life. To players that don't know Vampire well, this is a use of blood that puts the entire methabolism of the vampire to work again. During this time he will blush, breath, wink, drink, sweat, everything a normal human being of his physical age should do, without need to concentrate. It already costs blood, a lot of blood to the less Humane.<br /> <br /> About Primal Urge being animal instincts going wild, yes and no. After all, animals don't have Primal Urge, it is a Fera thing. So it is sort of a mystical sense. Could be better used setting of the allarm for powers in use, like the even more powerful Supernatural Awareness of Demons do, maybe with some effectiveness to tell when someone is using, as an example, a hiding or illusion power. That way, Primal Urge could tell of the presence of an Obfuscated or Chimerstry-Hiden vampire, without pinpointing him. It isn't just a vampire, but one you SHOULD have noticed if not for his cursed powers.<br /> <br /> Either way, as I said, I do the way I do for the sake of interesting games. I don't see anything wrong with a high-difficulty dice roll revealing that something is off. If at least it doesn't tell what is off.<br /> <br /> By the way, I think the way animals react to vampires are much more similar to the way HUMANS react to Werewolfs. Sounds to me much more like a supernatural response, like an unnatural fear, more linked to animal purity than instincts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:21:26-07:00","id":742474,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> Since detecting Vampires with PU and gifts is the topic, some thoughts by a mainly VtM player, but we play crossovers often. Much depends on what perks and Disciplines (Vampire gifts) or not the Vampire possesses.<br /> Every Vampire can use his/her supernatural blood to get the metabolism working again for a time. The Vampire will breathe, have standard body heat, sweat, normal skin colour, etc., gaining the blush of Life.<br /> There is an advantage of the same name you can aquire, which means that your metabolism never really stopped. You have the above features, but it costs you nothing except the cost to buy the advantage and is always on.<br /> There is an advantage &quot;Inoffensive to animals&quot; which lets animals think of the Vampire like a normal human.<br /> For animals and Garou it becomes even more problematic if a Vampire has the Animalism discipline, which even a single level of makes you quite attractive to animals<br /> Vampires with Humanity 7+ (there are more of those than one might believe) won\u00b4t register on most &quot;warning scanners&quot; the Garou have. (Considering some level oddities of Humanity, I\u00b4d say 6+)<br /> Tremere and other Thaumaturges might have paths or rituals (like domino of life) which can help obfuscate their true nature.<br /> There is an advantage which gives a Vampire a normal humanlike aura.<br /> And not to forget the &quot;Sanctity&quot; advantage, doubly effective if the character in question is really a nice guy/girl. This advantage makes the character gain the label &quot;a nice one&quot;, because you have the vibes of one.<br /> <br /> These are just some things that play a role in detecting a Vampire. The true masters of the masquerade will not be found out with most Garou gifts. Vampires with all or most of these advantages are not the norm, but common enough that even cautious Garou might &quot;fuck up&quot; occationally.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:22:19-07:00","id":742665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=742474#post742474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hi!<br /> Since detecting Vampires with PU and gifts is the topic, some thoughts by a mainly VtM player, but we play crossovers often. Much depends on what perks and Disciplines (Vampire gifts) or not the Vampire possesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello!<br /> I'm assuming by the terms &quot;perks&quot; (and &quot;advantages&quot; later in the post) you are referring to Merits. If I'm incorrect, please let me know, as it informs my responses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=742474#post742474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Vampire can use his/her supernatural blood to get the metabolism working again for a time. The Vampire will breathe, have standard body heat, sweat, normal skin colour, etc., gaining the blush of Life.<br /> There is an advantage of the same name you can aquire, which means that your metabolism never really stopped. You have the above features, but it costs you nothing except the cost to buy the advantage and is always on.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know Blush of Life doesn't play into how animals instinctually react to vampires. It is meant to help with hunting mainly. So I'm not sure if it will have any affect on using Primal Urge. And it certainly doesn't do any good against Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=742474#post742474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There is an advantage &quot;Inoffensive to animals&quot; which lets animals think of the Vampire like a normal human.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually an interesting idea. I think this merit would help against Garou &quot;naturally&quot; being off put by such a vampire. Still, it wouldn't help at all against Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=742474#post742474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For animals and Garou it becomes even more problematic if a Vampire has the Animalism discipline, which even a single level of makes you quite attractive to animals</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement was always made in the books, but provides no mechanics for it, making it mostly just fluff. It seems to just cover what the &quot;Inoffensive to animals&quot; merit would be then. It is also worth noting that in several books it says Animalism tends to be less than helpful (sometimes useless) against Garou. Obviously Elder levels are not really included in that statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=742474#post742474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Vampires with Humanity 7+ (there are more of those than one might believe) won\u00b4t register on most &quot;warning scanners&quot; the Garou have. (Considering some level oddities of Humanity, I\u00b4d say 6+)</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement is somewhat incorrect. Having a high humanity rating helps against Sense Wyrm. It does not help at all against any of the other (albeit more rare) detecting Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=742474#post742474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremere and other Thaumaturges might have paths or rituals (like domino of life) which can help obfuscate their true nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgy can do basically anything so it's hard to have a solid helpful response for how powers would interact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=742474#post742474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an advantage which gives a Vampire a normal humanlike aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auras tend to be a vampire thing. There might be a gift or 2 that can sense or interact with auras. I can't remember off the top of my head. But in general, having a brighter (living) aura isn't going to help much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=742474#post742474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And not to forget the &quot;Sanctity&quot; advantage, doubly effective if the character in question is really a nice guy/girl. This advantage makes the character gain the label &quot;a nice one&quot;, because you have the vibes of one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with this one. What book is it from?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=742474#post742474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are just some things that play a role in detecting a Vampire. The true masters of the masquerade will not be found out with most Garou gifts. Vampires with all or most of these advantages are not the norm, but common enough that even cautious Garou might &quot;fuck up&quot; occationally.</div> </div> </div> </div>True masters of the Masquerade should never be coming into close proximity with Garou, and so cannot risk detection. Generally, if you are a vampire and you come face to face with a pack of Garou, you've already screwed up. If it's just a matter of passing one another on a the street, the chances of either party noticing the other could be quite slim. It usually takes actively looking for each other for something to come of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:38:58-07:00","id":743216,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> @idpersona<br /> <br /> My post was made with the above stated Bar situation in mind and the sometimes laughable overpowering of PU some players/STs seem fond of.<br /> As far as I know, the Sensing Gifts beside Sense Wyrm are quite rare, so the characters are unlucky to run into it.<br /> Sanctity is a Vampire merit. Most people will like and respect you, even those who cannot stand you will be less inlcined to do something to you, since you have &quot;good vibrations&quot;. You can crash this merit by trully appalling behaviour, but if the Vampire in question is really a nice guy/girl (as far as Vampires can be) this can be quite helpful for a long unlife. This even works on Garou, because it is some part of your being shining through. It won\u00b4t help in a combat situation and enemies of you will still work against you, but the danger of terminal antagonism is lessened. So in a bar meeting a Garou will think twice about going all rage, since this nice girl might be a leech, but she is - nice!<br /> As far as animalism goes, the effects on animals go way beyond inoffensive. Vampires with animalism get mostly positive reactions from animals and often attract them without even trying..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:25:19-07:00","id":743293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=743216#post743216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> <br /> @idpersona<br /> <br /> My post was made with the above stated Bar situation in mind and the sometimes laughable overpowering of PU some players/STs seem fond of.<br /> As far as I know, the Sensing Gifts beside Sense Wyrm are quite rare, so the characters are unlucky to run into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Sense Wyrm and Scent of the True Form are some of the most basic Gifts available. Also, overpowering something? Don't compare power ratings in glass houses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sanctity is a Vampire merit. Most people will like and respect you, even those who cannot stand you will be less inlcined to do something to you, since you have &quot;good vibrations&quot;. You can crash this merit by trully appalling behaviour, but if the Vampire in question is really a nice guy/girl (as far as Vampires can be) this can be quite helpful for a long unlife. This even works on Garou, because it is some part of your being shining through. It won\u00b4t help in a combat situation and enemies of you will still work against you, but the danger of terminal antagonism is lessened. So in a bar meeting a Garou will think twice about going all rage, since this nice girl might be a leech, but she is - nice!<br /> As far as animalism goes, the effects on animals go way beyond inoffensive. Vampires with animalism get mostly positive reactions from animals and often attract them without even trying.. </div> </div> </div>Of course, animals aren't half spirit, and V:tM almost never takes that part into account. Gnosis provokes feelings of loathing toward the undead, and the duplicitous reputation of vampires makes it unlikely any such vampire is going to be trusted if the secret gets out in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T18:22:19-07:00","id":743407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=743216#post743216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sanctity is a Vampire merit. Most people will like and respect you, even those who cannot stand you will be less inlcined to do something to you, since you have &quot;good vibrations&quot;. You can crash this merit by trully appalling behaviour, but if the Vampire in question is really a nice guy/girl (as far as Vampires can be) this can be quite helpful for a long unlife. This even works on Garou, because it is some part of your being shining through. It won\u00b4t help in a combat situation and enemies of you will still work against you, but the danger of terminal antagonism is lessened. So in a bar meeting a Garou will think twice about going all rage, since this nice girl might be a leech, but she is - nice!<br /> As far as animalism goes, the effects on animals go way beyond inoffensive. Vampires with animalism get mostly positive reactions from animals and often attract them without even trying...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy. That sounds so hilarious in the context of Werewolf. Let's just say that those statements only apply to playing Vampire games.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T19:24:52-07:00","id":743491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=743216#post743216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> (since) the Vampire in question is really a nice guy/girl (as far as Vampires can be) this can be quite helpful for a long unlife. This even works on Garou, because it is some part of your being shining through. It won\u00b4t help in a combat situation and enemies of you will still work against you, but the danger of terminal antagonism is lessened. So in a bar meeting a Garou will think twice about going all rage, since this nice girl might be a leech, but she is - nice!</div> </div> </div> </div>Best case scenario, the Garou feels a twinge of remorse after tearing her pleasant undead head off. Even then, the line of thinking would probably be akin to 'it's terrible that the vamps had to befoul someone like that,' rather than 'killing this abomination makes me feel sad.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:17:11-07:00","id":743591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=743491#post743491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Best case scenario, the Garou feels a twinge of remorse after tearing her pleasant undead head off. Even then, the line of thinking would probably be akin to 'it's terrible that the vamps had to befoul someone like that,' rather than 'killing this abomination makes me feel sad.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see an especially young and naive Garou possibly thinking he/she could save said vampire, assuming the merit works as described (I have never heard of it, and don't know how it actually works). This assumption would quickly be corrected by any more experienced Garou.<br /> <br /> There are reasons vampires cannot be trusted, even besides them being of the Wyrm. I've played in games where my (or the player's) pack has allied with a singular vampire that they knew wasn't like every other vampire. Said special vampire wasn't corrupt or evil at all, and had the best of intentions. They just got unlucky one day and now was stuck in this undead state, but they were doing their best to get by without hurting anyone. <br /> Each and every single time it bit the pack in the ass. Twice the vampire turned out to be lying to and manipulating the pack. The third one did actually mean well, but was being manipulated by an Elder vampire to draw the pack out into the open to be slaughtered.<br /> Each time, every surviving pack member took the lesson to heart.<br /> In the end though it is in the nature of the young (Garou in this case) to think they know better than their Elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T06:21:11-07:00","id":744318,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> Sanctity has been around under differing names since VtM 2nd edition and is in V20 as well.<br /> Part of the effect is that you are trusted even if you are not trustworthy. While your enemies will keep on working against you, as long as you don\u00b4t offend them actively, they will not kill you.<br /> I find some of the above comments hilarious &quot;Raw Werewolves are immune to everything and even in a Bar with a chance encounter go all raw. No matter that the merit the Vamp has works on Werewolves as well. Raw all the time&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, let us kill this Vamp in a barfight, no matter that she kept the Park we revere pristine (and has a merit working on us we simply ignore that is so), because she liked it that way. Vamps can\u00b4t be trusted, so we kill her and the other bar visitors and later her succesor, who does not care about parks at all, can sell it to a Pentex subsidary. Werewolves go!<br /> Werewolves were once the immune system of Gaia, but now they are a leucemia, because of the terminal stupidity on longterm thinking 80% exhibit, which is unfortunately how WtA depicts them since 2nd edition.<br /> From the Werewlof side Vampires might not be trusted, but that is partly the work of the Shifters as well. Since Shifters attack Humans, Vampires with no reason, no rhyme from their perspectives, Humans and Vampires are united in their tries to keep these &quot;monsters&quot; at bay. While a &quot;Batfang&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Vampire is very rare, they and even some more selfish but humane Vamps did more for humanity and Gaia than the Werewolves do today. That is the main tragedy, because the Werewolves are too stuck in their ways and most think too little about the world as a whole, they are now part of the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","user":"G\u00fcnther","date":". 10-31-2015, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T07:30:17-07:00","id":744433,"title":"","content":"What you call unfortunate I call the core thesis of the game. Yeah, werewolves are trigger-happy and shortsighted and proud and it constnatly screws them over. They have all thsoe cautionary tales about the Impergium, the Wars of Rage, the War of Tears, the fall of the Howlers and yet they still keep screwing up for the same reasons. It's part of what makes Werewolf so compelling to play; they are not just furry superheroes, they are people with very real and in some cases very damning flaws.<br /> Vampires are just as indefensible though. And while in theory werewolves would love for everyone of them to fall off the Earth the reality of the fact is that werewolves will ignore, or sometimes deal with, the vampires whose trasgressions are minor. As long as your park-loving vampire doesn't murder (too much), doesn't kiss Kinfolk and more importantly looks like more trouble than its worth as a target the wolves will rather go after the youngsters who are bleeding teenagers dry during raves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T07:56:57-07:00","id":744480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=744318#post744318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> <br /> Sanctity has been around under differing names since VtM 2nd edition and is in V20 as well.<br /> Part of the effect is that you are trusted even if you are not trustworthy. While your enemies will keep on working against you, as long as you don\u00b4t offend them actively, they will not kill you.<br /> I find some of the above comments hilarious &quot;Raw Werewolves are immune to everything and even in a Bar with a chance encounter go all raw. No matter that the merit the Vamp has works on Werewolves as well. Raw all the time&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, let us kill this Vamp in a barfight, no matter that she kept the Park we revere pristine (and has a merit working on us we simply ignore that is so), because she liked it that way. Vamps can\u00b4t be trusted, so we kill her and the other bar visitors and later her succesor, who does not care about parks at all, can sell it to a Pentex subsidary. Werewolves go!<br /> Werewolves were once the immune system of Gaia, but now they are a leucemia, because of the terminal stupidity on longterm thinking 80% exhibit, which is unfortunately how WtA depicts them since 2nd edition.<br /> From the Werewlof side Vampires might not be trusted, but that is partly the work of the Shifters as well. Since Shifters attack Humans, Vampires with no reason, no rhyme from their perspectives, Humans and Vampires are united in their tries to keep these &quot;monsters&quot; at bay. While a &quot;Batfang&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Vampire is very rare, they and even some more selfish but humane Vamps did more for humanity and Gaia than the Werewolves do today. That is the main tragedy, because the Werewolves are too stuck in their ways and most think too little about the world as a whole, they are now part of the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just let's make this clear: If you're a werewolf, and you revere a park, there is something wrong with you on a basic level. Whipped cream on a turd is still shitty, and a park in a city does not make it a &quot;gaian place&quot; in their eyes. Sure, it's a slight improvement, but not that different, and sure as shit smells like a bribe. A vampire that sponsors large natural reserves would maybe be different, but then again werewolves are not known for performing extensive background checks on their enemies before attacking. Beeing rage-fueled and highly instinctual, conversations with vampires other than in-battle-snarls and screams are rare in my experience, and research is often minimal for such cases - and making your case while being attacked is hard to do when a few quick strikes is enough to kill you.<br /> <br /> Vampires are inherently tainted (and show up as red flags on several detection gifts), and any werewolf admitting to having discovered and not at least attempted to kill one will suffer for it, either through loss of reknown or general distrust, that is unless their sept is extremely progressive and open to new ideas. As this is highly unlikely, vampires tend to be killed, but not in a damn bar. Most werewolves would track them to their haven for a chance of a &quot;two-or-more birds with one stone&quot;-scenario, as one vampire is not really that impressive to bring to the next moot to gain reknown. Warforms in bars is extremely bad in the world of cameras, smartphones and general witnesses, even by the ridiculously simple and few rules werewolves live by - if they did do it there, that would mean a death sentence for everyone in the bar, and a difficult job making it &quot;look like an accident&quot; afterwards.<br /> <br /> That being said, &quot;Sanctity&quot; would perhaps be effective to a degree, and would create interesting scenarios for the werewolves that would encounter it. But an intelligent vampire would count his blessings after surviving an encounter with a pack, and not bet on this as a failsafe for further involvement with werewolves. Primal Urge could tell the garou that something was wrong, but not neccesarily what was wrong - this is an ability that determines how instinctually attuned a werewolf is, and should not be confused with a magical power the way I see it. A high rating might give you an indication, but a normal rating would be useless against something like this. Sanctity's efficiency would depend highly on how it functions - I wish someone could post it word by word, so we could see the exact phrasing of the merit.<br /> <br /> In general, werewolves answered the question &quot;Can vampires be good?&quot; ages ago with a resounding &quot;NO&quot;, and even though the possibility is sometimes entertained, they are generally considered &quot;kill on sight&quot;. Very little benefit of the doubt is generelly given to those who are proven to be vampires.<br /> Is this smart? Maybe not, but werewolves are not known for their intelligence and calm, reflected nature. But is it the way they have dealt with things for a long time, and they keep seeing taint wherever there are vampires, further reinforcing their position on their old enemies. I'd even go so far as to say that most garou would tear a Golconda-vamp to shreds simply because &quot;It's probably just a vampire-trick&quot; or &quot;I've smelled vampires in the caern before, this gift is not an exact science, better kill him to be sure&quot;.<br /> <br /> And your bit about vampires having done more for humanity than werewolves? Of course they have. Any parasite who is happy with the status quo will seek to preserve it's host. The fact is that humanity is not on most werewolves' &quot;friends list&quot;, and many regard them as a danger to Gaia in general, on both a physical and spiritual level. Werewolves allowed them to grow forth, and despite a reduction in taint among their own after the culling of the impergium stopped, this is generally regarded as having been a stupid decision among the vast majority of werewolves. They are however hard pressed when asked for an alternative solution, so they do the best with what they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9021-jeremiah-songkeeper","name":"Jeremiah Songkeeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T13:25:34-07:00","id":744939,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> @Vidyaraja, Jeremiah songkeeper<br /> <br /> Part of my post was meant as a hunourous answer to all that &quot;Werewolf Charge!!!&quot; posts,which totally disregarded some rules. While I like the &quot;core thesis&quot; of WtA, I still consider the way werewolves are depicted since 2nd edition as unfortunate. Being totally unable to change methods (and the authors purposely torpedoing the few tries for some sparks of intelligent change i.e. Dark Alliance:Vancouver) is not a good sign, because this makes you a living automaton.<br /> Werewolf can be very refreshing in it\u00b4s Hack and Slay approach after the neverending intrigues of VtM, but having put enemies in aggregate and methods set in stone by the authors screams for House rules IMHO.<br /> <br /> If your Vampire character is designed to be a nice guy/girl (as far as Vampires can be one), &quot;Sanctity&quot; is one of the most valuable and underestimated Merits you can take. If want to play a bastard it is too expensive since it will burn out fast due to your general behaviour, but if it fits your character design it is top. With the Sanctity you radiate the &quot;vibrations&quot; of being a nice, trustworthy person to anybody. Even Werewolves are affected because it is not a gift or discipline at work, only actively(!) showing yourself untrustworthy repeatedly cancels out this merit.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are written to be f++++++ tough (even tougher than in the basic real world legends), so combat solutions are logically front row ones, but I find it unrealistic that not a single high-ranking Leader came to the conclusion that we do like we always do and what happens? We lose and keep on losing, Maybe we should change something. Despite being squishy the Humans and Vampires still win most of the times in the end. Maybe we should begin to gather information on who among those two pests are more toleable than the rest.<br /> <br /> In our Vampire group, we play x-overs not too often, but regulary since we have Fast and Guest players who are really good WtA players. Starting from the VtM perspective this is a lot easier than from WtA, since most Vampires do not hate the Werewolves, they simply consider them a threat. In our group, Vamps and Wolfs do not hug each other, it is more a business treaty: You are there, we are here, these are the offical routes we use to traverse each others territory. &quot;Visiting rights&quot; for places are regulated and dedicated envoys are there to keep contact when needed. Some &quot;Elysium&quot; areas are declared. We did not change the basic outlocks of the two factions, there is mostly little love lost, but both sides use their brains to see that this &quot;co-existence&quot; beats the alternatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:48:15-07:00","id":745440,"title":"","content":"Vampires are a disease. Parasites that have infiltrated humanity and treat them like toys or even worse like cattle. This same group of entities spends their significantly long lives scheming, manipulating and fucking over each other and anything the other may own - including any and all human followers, organisations or interests. Explain to me how that is improving the human condition? Sure, they can have cool powers and alien mindsets that can impress you. But never, ever think that they are &quot;nice&quot;.<br /> <br /> What you seem to be missing about the way Werewolves operate is that they have quite a complex mileau in which they have loads of religious, spiritual, diplomatic, social and organisational interaction. They have whole orders of spirits, human beings strange places, other breeds, Caerns, septs, nations and tribes. They have enough problems handling their own problems to compound them with relationships with a group of well known backstabbers who are actually on their list of &quot;Things to kill according to the word of God(dess)). You do not give your enemies the rope to hang yourself.<br /> <br /> Your hypotetical &quot;Nice Guy&quot; with a merit that makes him look nice and trustworthy is all nice, but the moment the Garou realise what he is and what he does... he is going to be murdered. Not because they believe he is a &quot;bad guy&quot;, but because they believe they are doing him a favour. They are sure you are a nice guy, it makes it even more horrible how they have to kill you, to save you from the horror you have become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:53:59-07:00","id":745447,"title":"","content":"Save your time cogliostro, it's Chinatown. Some people just want to live the fantasy that all the factions in Owod are super secret besties deep down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T18:37:17-07:00","id":745510,"title":"","content":"Note that sanctity says &quot;<i>at the storyteller's discretion,</i> you tend to receive lesser punishments for wrongdoing, and are liked by most.&quot; A storyteller can easily determine that a werewolf isn't going to slow down in response to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T08:56:43-08:00","id":746712,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> @Resplendent Fire<br /> I know that, my bar example was just meant to highlight the ludicrousness of the &quot;Charge Werewolf! Rage, Rage all the time, frack the rules!&quot; posts and the stupidity of some factions trying to sell us that the Doggies after millenia of doing things one way and losing steadily, do not try some new ideas.<br /> <br /> @Cogliostro<br /> I do not miss that the Werewolves have a unique society with it\u00b4s own factions and interactions with spirits, etc, but it is still glaringly obvious that they have become part of the problem the WoD has. Since millenia they plan and fight a certain way and they mostly lose steadily. The Wolves even recognise this, but do they change it? No! This is Darwin-Award-level stupidity, knowing that something goes wrong and not even trying a different solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T11:24:02-08:00","id":747087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=746712#post746712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> I do not miss that the Werewolves have a unique society with it\u00b4s own factions and interactions with spirits, etc, but it is still glaringly obvious that they have become part of the problem the WoD has. Since millenia they plan and fight a certain way and they mostly lose steadily. The Wolves even recognise this, but do they change it? No! This is Darwin-Award-level stupidity, knowing that something goes wrong and not even trying a different solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were made to be brutal killers to counter the same on the opposite side. If they don't do particularly well with alternatives, that's because the metatext was &quot;this game is made to make violence easy and cathartic but not any less terrible&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, do you know what changing the world for the better would be in Werewolf? Reconciling with the Mokole by banding together with the Corax <i>and exterminating all vampires</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T14:19:46-08:00","id":747452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=747087#post747087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do you know what changing the world for the better would be in Werewolf? Reconciling with the Mokole by banding together with the Corax <i>and exterminating all vampires</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best thing I've read in this thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T16:50:51-08:00","id":750283,"title":"","content":"Fun times all around.<br /> <br /> Having read up on Sanctity, I'd say it's reasonably effective against young and non-fanatical Garou, both for avoiding detection because you don't seem like the type they'd imagine as a vampire and for pleading for mercy if you're detected anyway. Against experienced (or well-indoctrinated) werewolves, it still puts you a little lower on the radar, but any mercy is going to come in the form of &quot;Sorry, kid, you really didn't deserve what your sire did to you, but...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:55:42-08:00","id":750359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=750283#post750283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun times all around.<br /> <br /> Having read up on Sanctity, I'd say it's reasonably effective against young and non-fanatical Garou, both for avoiding detection because you don't seem like the type they'd imagine as a vampire and for pleading for mercy if you're detected anyway. Against experienced (or well-indoctrinated) werewolves, it still puts you a little lower on the radar, but any mercy is going to come in the form of &quot;Sorry, kid, you really didn't deserve what your sire did to you, but...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Indoctrination has less to do with it than how much the Garou values the continued goodwill of the spirits, which, at least for the ones that aren't corrupt, don't want vampires around. Some higher-Gnosis werewolves might also feel in a nearly palpable sense the utter wrongness of the vampire, though that's more of a thing that should be there in terms of mechanics than one that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T18:57:56-08:00","id":750415,"title":"","content":"The sum total of &quot;wrongness sensed by werewolves is Humanity 6- vampires who show up on sense wyrm and werewolves being able to smell that vampires aren't human (the smell of blood, decay, etc.) but just straight up &quot;utter wrongness sense&quot; is silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T19:08:10-08:00","id":750424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=750415#post750415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sum total of &amp;quot;wrongness sensed by werewolves is Humanity 6- vampires who show up on sense wyrm and werewolves being able to smell that vampires aren't human (the smell of blood, decay, etc.) but just straight up &amp;quot;utter wrongness sense&amp;quot; is silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but in the context of Werewolf it makes absolute sense. Vampires by their very nature will want to expand cities at the cost of the wilderness. The debate aside on the Vampire forum on small town existence most vampires want to expand cities as it herds the cattle closer together and makes feeding much easier. Werewolves and by extension the rest of the Changing Breeds with the exception of the Ananasi need the open space of wilderness for their animal breeds to prosper. This in my opinion just adds to the tension between Vampires and Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> Note I personally have no problem with the idea of a &quot;grand alliance&quot; between Garou, Molkoe, Corax, and Bubasti to utterly annihilate the leeches once and for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T19:45:29-08:00","id":750488,"title":"","content":"Doing things the werewolves don't like shouldn't mean &quot;They sense automatically as wrong with no gifts whatsoever.&quot; I have never even tried to dispute the antagonism or reasons for hating vampires, I just think people push it too hard to make it baked into the world's metaphysics. Going from &quot;Some of them show up as wyrm-tainted&quot; to &quot;they're intrinsically of the wyrm and high humanity only hides the taint&quot; or &quot;High gnosis werewolves should be able to automatically sense the wrongness that vampires are&quot; is a bit much.<br /> <br /> I also rather wish the original core book and ensuing supplements hadn't pushed the antagonism so hard because discussions like these are tiresome. One of the best things Werewolf: The Forsaken did was abandon it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-02-2015, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T20:18:59-08:00","id":750556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=750488#post750488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing things the werewolves don't like shouldn't mean &quot;They sense automatically as wrong with no gifts whatsoever.&quot; I have never even tried to dispute the antagonism or reasons for hating vampires, I just think people push it too hard to make it baked into the world's metaphysics. Going from &quot;Some of them show up as wyrm-tainted&quot; to &quot;they're intrinsically of the wyrm and high humanity only hides the taint&quot; or &quot;High gnosis werewolves should be able to automatically sense the wrongness that vampires are&quot; is a bit much.<br /> <br /> I also rather wish the original core book and ensuing supplements hadn't pushed the antagonism so hard because discussions like these are tiresome. One of the best things Werewolf: The Forsaken did was abandon it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that, again, it would follow with the way Werewolf lore considers vampires, in tandem with what Gnosis is (a connection to the living spiritual cosmos). It wouldn't be mechanically different from Predator;s Taint and nWoD vampires and werewolves automatically considering each other threats upon meeting, in some respects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T23:34:29-08:00","id":750779,"title":"","content":"It doesn't follow with the mechanics that actually exist. And what werewolves believe about vampires is not likely entirely true. They <i>don't</i> have all the answers as much as many Apocalypse fans think they do.<br /> <br /> Also, getting an alliance going to kill all vampires sounds like such a great idea, because such wars have <i>never</i> bitten the werewolves on the ass before. It's almost like one such war would be the biggest obstacle to such an alliance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T00:22:06-08:00","id":750799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=750779#post750779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't follow with the mechanics that actually exist. And what werewolves believe about vampires is not likely entirely true. They <i>don't</i> have all the answers as much as many Apocalypse fans think they do.<br /> <br /> Also, getting an alliance going to kill all vampires sounds like such a great idea, because such wars have <i>never</i> bitten the werewolves on the ass before. It's almost like one such war would be the biggest obstacle to such an alliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, everything's been going pretty swell in Egypt since the Strider Crusade. Mokole and Bubasti are communicating and participating, and the Setites are not in the best of places. The whole thing was seen as one of the linchpins for Walks With Might's work with the Ahadi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T01:45:25-08:00","id":750945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=750779#post750779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't follow with the mechanics that actually exist. And what werewolves believe about vampires is not likely entirely true. They <i>don't</i> have all the answers as much as many Apocalypse fans think they do.<br /> <br /> Also, getting an alliance going to kill all vampires sounds like such a great idea, because such wars have <i>never</i> bitten the werewolves on the ass before. It's almost like one such war would be the biggest obstacle to such an alliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> This is one of the biggest &quot;beefs&quot; I have with all this &quot;Werewolf Yeehaw! Rage! Rage! We know everything, sense everything!&quot; crap posts disregarding all rules as well. An example: Among my WoD characters the one with the most heart\u00b4s blood in it, is a Tremere I have played for many years, from still being a human (we always played the Embrace out back then) to the Elder and deputy Primogen (he would normally be the Primogen but his duties to House and Clan take a lot of time) he is today. This Tremere has the Sanctity, Eat Food &quot;Masquerade-relating&quot; advantages, his skin is pale but still in the human range (aren\u00b4t disciplines and Thau great<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />?) and does not show up on Sense Wyrm, since a truckload of tough in-game decisions and some XP-expense kept my character\u00b4s Humanity high. Rulewise, even fluffwise there is zero chance that a Garou would sense anything amiss in a casual one-evening meeting in a bar, even if some Doggie cheerleaders dream of it. And there are a lot of PC and NPC (official ones too) out there who have even more masquerade-strenghtening skills and merits than my Tremere does.<br /> <br /> @saur ops Specialist<br /> <br /> Do you know what would be another way to change the WtA world for the better?<br /> Among the Shifters, the Garou embody (in VtM terms) the worst traits of Brujah Antitribu Iconoclasts and Pander. They fucked over Humanity since the Impergium, even today innocent humans are only collateral in their thinking. And they fucked over their Shifter friends during the War of Rage and other occations. It is rather telling that other shifters are less inclined to rage when meeting a Vampire and some even have comparatively friendly relations on case to case basis.<br /> <br /> Finally putting down these stupid murderous bedside rugs would be good. With the Cats, Bears, Foxes or the Coyotes you can reason and push back and defeat Pentex. The majority of Vampires might be selfish (as said, &quot;Batfang and Robin&quot; types of Vampire are rare) and some are even bastards, but Pentex victorious wouldn\u00b4t be good for the Cainites most loved toy, meal, ressource, recruitment pool, sometimes even friend and lover: humanity.<br /> The majority of Vampires has a vested interest that Pentex does not win. But there is nobody who explains it to the Vampires. The Doggies are too dumb and fanatic to do anything but fight them. And even if a e.g. Bastet would find the ear of influential Vamps, the chances are &quot;good&quot; that that the idiot Garou would kill her for trafficing with &quot;the enemy&quot;.<br /> Unlike the Garou there are Vampires of all sects (less among the Sabbat, but Anarchs and Camarilla ones more) who could set back Pentex easier than all Werewolves combined, if they had the right incentive and knowledge of Pentex. That is something the Doggies never get, other Shifter do. After Pentex is brought down, if the two sides want it, they could still dish it out, but that ould be unlikely, since non-doggie Shifter have brains!. Unlike this leucemia of Gaia otherwise named Werewolves, there are intelligent shifters who could see that sometimes you have to jump over your own shadow to get desired results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T02:42:51-08:00","id":751007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=750799#post750799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, everything's been going pretty swell in Egypt since the Strider Crusade. Mokole and Bubasti are communicating and participating, and the Setites are not in the best of places. The whole thing was seen as one of the linchpins for Walks With Might's work with the Ahadi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Statistically, the odds are against it.<br /> <br /> Also, which book is that in? I want to read it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T02:45:50-08:00","id":751009,"title":"","content":"G\u00fcnther if you wish to celebrate Vampires you should probably head to the Vampire forum. Don't be surprised that people here aren't that keen on your interpretation, especially as you seem to be running on a number of misconception of what the Garou are actually like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","user":"Cogliostro","date":". 11-03-2015, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T02:47:46-08:00","id":751010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=751007#post751007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Statistically, the odds are against it.<br /> <br /> Also, which book is that in? I want to read it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Rage across Egypt and Rage across the World. It's pretty awesome, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T02:53:13-08:00","id":751012,"title":"","content":"Thanks - and I have no doubt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T06:37:06-08:00","id":751276,"title":"","content":"Changing Breed 20 covers the formation of the Ahadi. Changing Breed revised expands on Rage across Egypt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T07:01:15-08:00","id":751334,"title":"","content":"While all of the various splats inhabit something called the World of Darkness not all of these Worlds are necessarily the same. In your Vampire game the lupines are not Garou unless the storyteller says so.<br /> In Werewolf the myth of Caine is not the cause of vampires. Vampires were not cursed by Angels, there is no redemption through Golconda not promise of it. Not one of the various Changing Breeds consider Vampires among their close friends. Ananasi- the spider shifters that drink blood to power their gifts and lives consider Vampires to be rivals at best. Bastet consider Vampires as a source of secrets and targets of opportunity. Corax sacred duty to dance a little dance and bring sunshine to the night. Guhrahl can't heal them so they kill them. Kitsune blessed by Gaia so that they go up in flames if a vampire tries to embrace them, plus undead tricked the Beast Courts into war. Ajaba vampires weaken humanity, making more work for the Chosers of the slain no one likes more work. Nuwisha you are kidding, the coyotes love these guys especially their toys which they steal and trash. The Molkoe have major issues with every vampire that exists, tied to Helos killing Vampires ranks as a sacred duty and the Molkoe remember Egypt, the Slave Trade, and every single time a Vampire betrayed them. Ratkin might take a contract from them but the Ratkin don't like them and they really don't like their kin being coerced into slavery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T07:34:35-08:00","id":751401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=751009#post751009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">G\u00fcnther if you wish to celebrate Vampires you should probably head to the Vampire forum. Don't be surprised that people here aren't that keen on your interpretation, especially as you seem to be running on a number of misconception of what the Garou are actually like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> I do not specifically celebrate VtM, I have fun at the expense of the Doggie Super-Cheerleaders, who believe that the least cerebral bunch even among the Shifters, knows everything, senses everything, kills everything, despite the rules and mostly the fluff says otherwise.<br /> As far as misconceptions go, there are a lot among the WtA fans too. And it is very telling that a majority of those taking offence at my posts brabble about things I never wrote, never did say. I never wrote about Embraces of Doggies or close friendships, something some WtA &quot;fans&quot; try to put in my mouth. I wrote about enlightened self-interest, something the Garou are simply too stupid to reach for. Making a deal with the lesser evil to bring down the larger one.<br /> As for the Lores, some things the Super-fans claim to be true, is found nowhere in the books and personal conjecture at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T07:48:16-08:00","id":751413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=750945#post750945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hi!<br /> <br /> This is one of the biggest &quot;beefs&quot; I have with all this &quot;Werewolf Yeehaw! Rage! Rage! We know everything, sense everything!&quot; crap posts disregarding all rules as well. An example: Among my WoD characters the one with the most heart\u00b4s blood in it, is a Tremere I have played for many years, from still being a human (we always played the Embrace out back then) to the Elder and deputy Primogen (he would normally be the Primogen but his duties to House and Clan take a lot of time) he is today. This Tremere has the Sanctity, Eat Food &quot;Masquerade-relating&quot; advantages, his skin is pale but still in the human range (aren\u00b4t disciplines and Thau great<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />?) and does not show up on Sense Wyrm, since a truckload of tough in-game decisions and some XP-expense kept my character\u00b4s Humanity high. Rulewise, even fluffwise there is zero chance that a Garou would sense anything amiss in a casual one-evening meeting in a bar, even if some Doggie cheerleaders dream of it. And there are a lot of PC and NPC (official ones too) out there who have even more masquerade-strenghtening skills and merits than my Tremere does.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Again, why do you care? Vampire is a different game. It has nothing to do with spirits as Werewolf sets it up, and has a completely different set of concerns. The reason why we're not questioning the basic underpinnings of W:tA while disregarding others is because there isn't a single shared WoD. Go back to your lupines and stop worrying about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you know what would be another way to change the WtA world for the better?<br /> Among the Shifters, the Garou embody (in VtM terms) the worst traits of Brujah Antitribu Iconoclasts and Pander. They fucked over Humanity since the Impergium, even today innocent humans are only collateral in their thinking. And they fucked over their Shifter friends during the War of Rage and other occations. It is rather telling that other shifters are less inclined to rage when meeting a Vampire and some even have comparatively friendly relations on case to case basis. </div> </div> </div>Never start off a post comparing part of your own corner to bad things that the other side has done. Because vampires don't have the foresight or inclination to stop being bastards, and are arguably encouraged to keep being bastards where other factors would discourage it for Garou and Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally putting down these stupid murderous bedside rugs would be good. With the Cats, Bears, Foxes or the Coyotes you can reason and push back and defeat Pentex. The majority of Vampires might be selfish (as said, &quot;Batfang and Robin&quot; types of Vampire are rare) and some are even bastards, but Pentex victorious wouldn\u00b4t be good for the Cainites most loved toy, meal, ressource, recruitment pool, sometimes even friend and lover: humanity. </div> </div> </div>That's absolutely hilarious. Pentex wants a tractable people who are willing to roll over and do whatever the company says. This is, at its most antagonistic, orthogonal to what vampires desire, which is to say, not very. The only reason a vampire would have a problem with it would be if they wanted vampires to run everything entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The majority of Vampires has a vested interest that Pentex does not win. But there is nobody who explains it to the Vampires. </div> </div> </div>See above. Also, no one typically explains Pentex to anyone, because it's a rather nondescript shell company holding a bunch of subsidiaries, and its name isn't actually commonplace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Doggies are too dumb and fanatic to do anything but fight them. And even if a e.g. Bastet would find the ear of influential Vamps, the chances are &quot;good&quot; that that the idiot Garou would kill her for trafficing with &quot;the enemy&quot;.<br /> Unlike the Garou there are Vampires of all sects (less among the Sabbat, but Anarchs and Camarilla ones more) who could set back Pentex easier than all Werewolves combined, if they had the right incentive and knowledge of Pentex. That is something the Doggies never get, other Shifter do. After Pentex is brought down, if the two sides want it, they could still dish it out, but that ould be unlikely, since non-doggie Shifter have brains!. Unlike this leucemia of Gaia otherwise named Werewolves, there are intelligent shifters who could see that sometimes you have to jump over your own shadow to get desired results. </div> </div> </div>Any Garou that's actually been acting against Pentex - which, by the way, most people don't know even exists - for any length of time actually knows the score, but W20 BotW made it clear that they're really, really entrenched in the modern corporate world. Vampires couldn't oust them, if there was some actual crossover reason to make them want to do so; mages can't oust them, since they don't have it in them to pull off anything that big in that short a time, in the event, again, that you want to engage in crossover. Demon never intersects with W:tA to begin with. This isn't their fight, and they aren't actually better suited to it, because while they don't have Rage, they also are much more subject to the temptation to just let leave anything that's good for humans in some fashion, even with horrible downsides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:19:16-08:00","id":751617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=751401#post751401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have fun at the expense of the Doggie Super-Cheerleaders</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, you are just being openly insulting to the fan base, while offering no real points for discussion. This is pretty much the definition of trolling.<br /> <br /> Vampires in WtA aren't necessarily organized at all, much less into the various sects from VtM. That is really worth remembering.<br /> Also, Vampires aren't likely to be able to take down Pentex, even if they knew about it. Any Vampire with enough resources to actually try would more likely attempt to take over, because that's how Vampires work. You don't destroy possible resources when you (theoretically) have the ability to acquire them instead.<br /> <br /> And the Garou don't attempt to forge alliances with Vampires en masse, because they have before. And each and every time it ends with dead Garou and possibly destroyed caerns. Every time. Without exception. Such is the nature of Vampires, even without taking into account the wyrm taint.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T13:43:45-08:00","id":752174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=751617#post751617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point, you are just being openly insulting to the fan base, while offering no real points for discussion. This is pretty much the definition of trolling.<br /> <br /> Vampires in WtA aren't necessarily organized at all, much less into the various sects from VtM. That is really worth remembering.<br /> Also, Vampires aren't likely to be able to take down Pentex, even if they knew about it. Any Vampire with enough resources to actually try would more likely attempt to take over, because that's how Vampires work. You don't destroy possible resources when you (theoretically) have the ability to acquire them instead.<br /> <br /> And the Garou don't attempt to forge alliances with Vampires en masse, because they have before. And each and every time it ends with dead Garou and possibly destroyed caerns. Every time. Without exception. Such is the nature of Vampires, even without taking into account the wyrm taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> The fanbase? I count several longtime (18+ years) WtA players among my friends! The &quot;DSC&quot; comment was directed at the posters who claim without rule or fluff support that Werewolves can find out Vampires from a full bar on first meet without any hints into the undead direction with &quot;feel&quot; alone. That is just believing hyperbole and not the only thing where part(!) of the WtA fanbase believe that Werewolves are the best in everything since sliced bread.<br /> <br /> VtM not WtA: Only if you use a strict borderline. Because the various systems play officially in the same universe, which would mean the Vampires are the Ivory Tower aka Camarilla, The Sword of Caine aka the Sabbat and tha Anarchs (We leave the small sects and outliers alone for a moment). Then a lot of the stuff about Vampires in WtA is simply fanatics crap.<br /> And I think this is why we are at odds here, because if the Vampires are VtM, then the Garou are nothing but terminally stupid, omnicidal fanatics, which derserve(!) to be put down, since they fuck over humanity to this day, fucked over the other Shifters several times and fucked over the Vampires because in VtM nearly all breakdowns of ceasefire started with a Garou snapping, going alll rage and breaking the truce until the Vampires retaliated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T14:23:00-08:00","id":752241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=752174#post752174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The fanbase? I count several longtime (18+ years) WtA players among my friends! The &quot;DSC&quot; comment was directed at the posters who claim without rule or fluff support that Werewolves can find out Vampires from a full bar on first meet without any hints into the undead direction with &quot;feel&quot; alone. That is just believing hyperbole and not the only thing where part(!) of the WtA fanbase believe that Werewolves are the best in everything since sliced bread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trolling and being insulting because you feel justified is still trolling and being insulting. In my experience, most WtA fans know that the Garou are flawed heroes. And fluff support was cited. You just don't agree with the reasoning (which is obviously fine). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=752174#post752174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> VtM not WtA: Only if you use a strict borderline. Because the various systems play officially in the same universe, which would mean the Vampires are the Ivory Tower aka Camarilla, The Sword of Caine aka the Sabbat and tha Anarchs (We leave the small sects and outliers alone for a moment). Then a lot of the stuff about Vampires in WtA is simply fanatics crap.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't necessarily agree. Depending on the specific book, the universes can be quite different. Several core books specifically say to make up whatever powers you deem appropriate for a creature type, regardless of what their books say. This point however has been argued both way for several years, and isn't really the point on this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=752174#post752174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And I think this is why we are at odds here, because if the Vampires are VtM, then the Garou are nothing but terminally stupid, omnicidal fanatics, which derserve(!) to be put down, since they fuck over humanity to this day, fucked over the other Shifters several times and fucked over the Vampires because in VtM nearly all breakdowns of ceasefire started with a Garou snapping, going alll rage and breaking the truce until the Vampires retaliated.</div> </div> </div> </div>It tends to be a running theme that (most) every major splat in WoD doesn't care for individual human lives. The stance you are attributing to just Garou applies to Garou, Vampires (of all sects), Changelings (to a degree) and to the entirety of the Ascension War. Your point of view seems to most closely line up with the ideology in Hunter the Reckoning.<br /> Which isn't to say that there is anything wrong with that, but we are discussing the game from an out of game perspective. And this is a WtA, so people are going to be fans of the Garou. There are certainly fluff arguments to be made for detecting Vampires using a Garou's natural instincts and abilities. You disagree, and that is fine. There is no reason to be belligerent in your discussions though. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T14:56:35-08:00","id":752265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=752174#post752174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> VtM not WtA: Only if you use a strict borderline. Because the various systems play officially in the same universe, which would mean the Vampires are the Ivory Tower aka Camarilla, The Sword of Caine aka the Sabbat and tha Anarchs</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this right here is the source of a lot of nerd rage. Since you think the universes are shared, the Kindred, by defacto, are competing with the Garou.<br /> <br /> Which means the Kindred lose.<br /> <br /> Fact is, you can't compare Caine's dead grandbabbies to the terrestrial apex predators of planet earth. The Garou are quite literally at the top of the food chain within the confines of their own game. Werewolves practically have Cthulhu's stats from CoC when they fight vamps: roll a dice, that many die a turn. It isn't fair because it isn't supposed to be and it never was. If you want to mix it up, feel free to do so, but don't grouse at us because our favorite monsters are better at killing. It is only a competition if you make it one, and you clearly are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-05-2015, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T15:24:05-08:00","id":752278,"title":"","content":"<br /> \u00a1wow!<br /> <br /> One enter looking for information and find a loosy try of a flamewar... \u00a1how sweet!<br /> Pls, let's stop feeding the troll.<br /> <br /> First thing first, the main splats - as our companions of NWoD would say - are different in the main books that aren't their own.<br /> Vampires in Werewolf, are cannon fodder, as easily as that, werewolfs in Vampire are cannon fodder too, rules are different in both games regarding the other, Werewolf rules in Vampire are nonexistent, werewolf in a Vampire game only exist for being anihilated, if the rules and fluff doesn't say anything more about them - and I'm talking about the older editions not V20, I don't have the book- one doesn't even care anymore than that. For Werewolf is the same about vampires.<br /> <br /> Fluff aside, in both books there are no rules to build the other, in the antagonist section of W20 for example, vampires got sugested gifts to emulate their disciplices, and in V20, Werewolfs have disciplines to emulate their power.<br /> <br /> CWoD initally is not crossover frienly, base games dont tell you anything about others, fluff books only tell you about the other in an atagonistic or neutral light because the fluff books of a game doesn't even care about the fluff books of that other game, easy as that. <br /> <br /> Let's talk about that dichtonomy, let's talk about that flute again: the Harmony Flute.<br /> Rules say thar creatures without rage cannont resist its effects, let's see this hypothetical close room case, or white room, or whatever.<br /> <br /> A vampire master will made his players roll willpower to resist the effects of the flute.<br /> A werewolf master initally don't do that for a bunch of npc only made to be slaughter.<br /> <br /> The games are not crossover friendly because every main faction is antagonistic about the other, as easy as that, and fluff of every book of their respective lines are writted with that in mind, werewolf books say that vampires are scum, vampire books say that werewolfs are mindless stupid beast, well, cool, no probs here, right?<br /> <br /> having clarified, what fluff and rules in a game book say about the other line doesn't correspond with the reality of the rules and fluff of that other line, let's gonna left the game's enmity inside their respectives games, and this case is closed.<br /> <br /> Any more stupid shit and I'm calling for a Moderator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nosolorol.com/nuevo/images/Fostern.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1192-aura","name":"Aura","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T17:20:21-08:00","id":752490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=752241#post752241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your point of view seems to most closely line up with the ideology in Hunter the Reckoning.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not even with Waywards, I'd wager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-03-2015, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T00:38:32-08:00","id":753271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=752265#post752265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, this right here is the source of a lot of nerd rage. Since you think the universes are shared, the Kindred, by defacto, are competing with the Garou.<br /> Which means the Kindred lose.<br /> Fact is, you can't compare the Caine's dead grandbabbies to the terrestrial apex predators of planet earth. The Garou are quite literally at the top of the food chain within the confines of their own game. Werewolves practically have Cthulhu's stats from CoC when they fight vamps: roll a dice, that many die a turn. It isn't fair because it isn't supposed to be and it never was. If you want to mix it up, feel free to do so, but don't grouse at us because our favorite monsters are better at killing. It is only a competition if you make it one, and you clearly are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> The Kindred only lose in one-on-one or pack fights, their specific advantages lie in other things. But your post sums up that you do not understand what the earnest meant parts of my posts are about. You and the majority of the other posters attacking me think it is about killing power, but that is not even close.<br /> I quipped about combat to tease the &quot;RAWWRR Werewolves for the win no matter what&quot; crowd, getting them in &quot;Red Talon mode&quot;, but the real meat of this discussion for me is the implausible staticness of Garou thinking. (The old authors should knew better) The Werewolves have a Plan A and that Plan is B, C, D, etc as well. That is even more static than the already laughable supposed stasis of the Kindred was in old editions and it was well received in V20, that they lifted that implausabilty with the explanation that many old Vampires are simply set in their ways but can and do learn new things easily if they want or have incentive to.<br /> Now for WtA, I hoped that they would lift the totally stuck ways of the Garou at least partially as well. And it does not matter, if it is about Vampires, Mages, normal Humans or Santa Claus. It is the fact that the Werewolves know something is not right how they go about protecting Gaia. They are losing step by step, but do not try for different solutions. That is an equal facepalm by the old authors as was the total stasis of the Cainites. I hope this clears it up for you a bit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T04:15:16-08:00","id":753645,"title":"","content":"Again. You have a very specific view of how the world works. It's your headcanon and it's fine for your games, but it's not how Werewolf works. It's a stance that does not gel with the setting as presented and it's a stance that's not going to gel with people actually playing Werewolf on its own merits without crossovering everything into love and peace.<br /> <br /> So do be a dear, and stop trying to brainwash us into agreeing with you. You have nothing to clear up to us, we get our own game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:34:17-08:00","id":754601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/576222-garou-leech-kiss-ecstasy?p=753271#post753271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> <br /> The Kindred only lose in one-on-one or pack fights, their specific advantages lie in other things. But your post sums up that you do not understand what the earnest meant parts of my posts are about. You and the majority of the other posters attacking me think it is about killing power, but that is not even close.<br /> I quipped about combat to tease the &quot;RAWWRR Werewolves for the win no matter what&quot; crowd, getting them in &quot;Red Talon mode&quot;, but the real meat of this discussion for me is the implausible staticness of Garou thinking. (The old authors should knew better) The Werewolves have a Plan A and that Plan is B, C, D, etc as well. That is even more static than the already laughable supposed stasis of the Kindred was in old editions and it was well received in V20, that they lifted that implausabilty with the explanation that many old Vampires are simply set in their ways but can and do learn new things easily if they want or have incentive to.<br /> Now for WtA, I hoped that they would lift the totally stuck ways of the Garou at least partially as well. And it does not matter, if it is about Vampires, Mages, normal Humans or Santa Claus. It is the fact that the Werewolves know something is not right how they go about protecting Gaia. They are losing step by step, but do not try for different solutions. That is an equal facepalm by the old authors as was the total stasis of the Cainites. I hope this clears it up for you a bit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We already know what the shortcomings of the protagonist group of the game are; the game itself acknowledges this out of character, and also sets up a setting where the struggle is in turning things around and getting to the ultimate causes of ills rather than dealing with proximate issues. This isn't a new and groundbreaking conversation. You aren't clearing anything up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}